# The native clang-tidy checks (D00 T05 §4), run by scripts/native-tidy.ps1 over the x64 Debug compile database: the
# seven families the spec names ("Warnings and analysis"), every warning an error, and headers reported only when they
# live under native/ and outside the build tree; scripts/native-tidy.ps1 removes the two MSVC switches clang-cl does not
# implement. Each exclusion and its reason:
#   modernize-use-trailing-return-type: the house style declares the return type first (D00 T04 §1).
#   cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers, readability-magic-numbers: imaging code is full of format-defined constants;
#     review asks for a named constant where a value carries meaning, which a lexical check cannot tell.
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once: the suite builds with MSVC only, which supports #pragma once.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '[/\\]native[/\\]'
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '[/\\]artifacts[/\\]'
